invariant: INV-16
file: poly1305_ifma.c
catches: poly1305_equiv_test
reason: multiply_add adds a2 times r2 at 2^44 rather than a2 times 20 r2,
  the part of the product at 2^176 that is 20 2^44 modulo 2^130 - 5, so
  every product the kernel computes is wrong and so is the tag.
  bin/poly1305_equiv_test runs the kernel's own text over the lane model
  on every host and compares it with poly1305.c's loop.

--- old
    lo[1] = lanes_multiply_add_low(lo[1], a[2], by->s2);
--- new
    lo[1] = lanes_multiply_add_low(lo[1], a[2], by->r2);
